WEBVTT

00:12.053 --> 00:13.805
♪ See the daylight ♪

00:15.223 --> 00:17.392
♪ Covering the sky ♪

00:18.852 --> 00:22.230
♪ Hear the wind say ♪

00:22.313 --> 00:26.484
♪ No matter what you do, my friend ♪

00:26.568 --> 00:29.195
♪ You know the world
Still needs your light ♪

00:29.279 --> 00:32.449
♪ Let it just shine ♪

00:32.532 --> 00:34.951
♪ You'll be free ♪

00:35.035 --> 00:38.204
♪ From all the things you used to be ♪

00:40.040 --> 00:41.833
[curious music playing]

00:43.877 --> 00:48.590
DOONA!

01:05.607 --> 01:08.109
[Doona] If you don't like it,
you can pull your hand away.

01:15.867 --> 01:17.869
[emotional music playing]

01:25.710 --> 01:26.544
[sighs]

01:50.151 --> 01:54.948
EPISODE 4
THE UNEXPECTED

01:57.867 --> 01:59.828
[gentle music playing]

02:01.746 --> 02:06.626
WATER FILTRATION PLANT PLANNING
FILTRATION TARGET PARTICULATE MATTER

02:17.762 --> 02:20.473
WOLMI THEME PARK
STAFF

02:24.352 --> 02:26.479
[robotic voice] Sorry,
the number you're trying to reach

02:26.563 --> 02:27.647
is currently unavailable.

02:27.730 --> 02:29.440
- Please try again later.
- [sighs]

02:41.870 --> 02:42.704
[locker beeps]

03:11.858 --> 03:13.318
When do you take your lunch break?

03:14.027 --> 03:16.237
Oh, um, I don't think
I have time for lunch today.

03:16.321 --> 03:17.280
Seriously?

03:18.698 --> 03:20.074
That's disappointing.

03:20.158 --> 03:21.784
Mmm, sorry, Doona.

03:22.493 --> 03:25.079
[chuckles] Why do you
always apologize for everything?

03:26.873 --> 03:31.085
Okay, look, no need to worry about me.
I didn't come here to see you anyway.

03:32.170 --> 03:33.421
Doing things alone is fun.

03:36.090 --> 03:38.092
[guests screaming]

03:39.636 --> 03:41.638
[screaming]

03:45.975 --> 03:47.894
[man] The ride will begin momentarily.

03:47.977 --> 03:50.480
To all passengers,
please pull down the safety bar

03:50.563 --> 03:51.940
down to your waist until it clicks.

03:52.023 --> 03:53.524
- Thank you.
- Whoo!

03:54.025 --> 03:55.318
Whoo!

04:02.492 --> 04:03.326
[sniffs]

04:05.787 --> 04:07.997
Whoo!

04:08.581 --> 04:10.959
Wow, this is actually not fun at all.

04:13.419 --> 04:15.421
[emotional music playing]

04:54.919 --> 04:56.504
Oh! Are you done?

05:04.595 --> 05:06.014
[slurping]

05:11.644 --> 05:13.354
You're just loving that meal, aren't you?

05:13.938 --> 05:16.107
I haven't been able
to eat anything all day.

05:16.941 --> 05:18.943
[slurping]

05:20.361 --> 05:21.321
[chuckles softly]

05:23.489 --> 05:24.866
Once, there was this concert I had.

05:27.076 --> 05:28.911
It got canceled due to the weather.

05:30.371 --> 05:32.540
If felt like a gift, you know?

05:32.623 --> 05:34.959
I found myself
having all this free time for once.

05:35.543 --> 05:38.129
So I really wanted
to do something special with it.

05:38.713 --> 05:40.548
But I couldn't figure out what to do.

05:42.425 --> 05:43.843
At the time, I didn't know why.

05:45.053 --> 05:47.513
Then the day came when I realized,

05:48.431 --> 05:50.850
aside from singing
and performing on stage,

05:51.768 --> 05:54.020
I had never done anything else in my life.

05:55.938 --> 05:56.856
[chuckles softly]

05:59.067 --> 06:00.401
It wasn't until later

06:01.527 --> 06:02.904
I began to wonder a lot.

06:03.946 --> 06:06.824
What would happen if I couldn't sing
or perform onstage anymore?

06:07.992 --> 06:09.869
What would become of my life then?

06:10.453 --> 06:11.746
Who is Lee Doona?

06:13.289 --> 06:14.499
I didn't know myself.

06:15.249 --> 06:16.209
I felt alone.

06:17.794 --> 06:19.879
What if I could never amount to anything?

06:23.883 --> 06:24.717
Anyways,

06:26.052 --> 06:28.304
I think I'm doing
a lot better than I thought.

06:28.388 --> 06:29.972
Although, I'm still figuring it out.

06:31.015 --> 06:31.849
Glad to hear that.

06:32.975 --> 06:33.851
[chuckles softly]

06:36.145 --> 06:37.605
KOREAN HISTORY, TOEIC MASTERY

06:37.688 --> 06:38.898
How about you?

06:39.690 --> 06:40.817
What are your aspirations?

06:40.900 --> 06:43.653
I assume your dream wasn't
to overwork yourself every day.

06:46.030 --> 06:47.407
Uh,

06:47.490 --> 06:49.325
we're here
eating jajangmyeon late at night,

06:49.409 --> 06:51.160
so, um, isn't that enough of a win?

06:52.245 --> 06:53.246
[chuckles]

06:54.747 --> 06:58.668
For me, um, living a normal life
is all I've ever really wanted, you know?

07:00.420 --> 07:01.838
That's enough for me, I think.

07:03.339 --> 07:04.424
[slurping]

07:12.098 --> 07:13.266
Have a fortune cookie.

07:18.980 --> 07:20.815
Here's hoping one of us will be lucky.

07:28.322 --> 07:29.449
[Won-jun] Huh…

07:34.245 --> 07:35.538
Hold on, um…

07:35.621 --> 07:37.665
I thought fortunes
were supposed to be positive.

07:38.249 --> 07:39.417
Who made these?

07:39.500 --> 07:40.418
What's it say?

07:40.501 --> 07:41.919
"You will face your worst enemy,

07:42.003 --> 07:44.547
and you'll be as helpless
as a mouse is to a cat."

07:44.630 --> 07:46.674
[chuckles] Are you the mouse?

07:46.757 --> 07:48.176
[laughs]

07:48.259 --> 07:50.678
"So you should prepare
for the unexpected soon,

07:50.761 --> 07:52.638
or else the consequences
could be super dire."

07:52.722 --> 07:54.807
So much for trying to lighten things up.

07:55.766 --> 07:56.601
Maybe next time.

07:56.684 --> 07:58.186
[sighs] It's all right.

07:58.978 --> 08:01.189
I never make enemies,
so I'm not worried at all.

08:02.064 --> 08:02.899
That's true.

08:06.569 --> 08:07.862
I'm in a good mood, anyway…

08:10.907 --> 08:12.658
'cause this is some good jajangmyeon.

08:14.911 --> 08:15.786
Also true.

08:16.537 --> 08:17.580
[Won-jun slurping]

08:20.917 --> 08:23.753
- How about we have another date sometime?
- Like when?

08:23.836 --> 08:26.088
On a day when the weather is so amazing,

08:26.797 --> 08:28.466
a day so good, we can't stay inside.

08:31.260 --> 08:32.970
[slurping]

08:36.224 --> 08:37.558
[Won-jun] This is so good.

08:43.314 --> 08:45.191
- Hey, Won-jun.
- Hmm?

08:46.526 --> 08:48.486
You shouldn't overwork so much.

08:51.030 --> 08:54.158
You're allowed to take it easy.
Take care of yourself for once.

08:55.493 --> 08:56.452
Just like I am.

08:58.204 --> 09:01.082
Relax a little here and there
and be lazy once in a while.

09:02.583 --> 09:03.584
Who cares, right?

09:07.964 --> 09:08.798
What?

09:10.216 --> 09:11.342
I do take it easy.

09:11.926 --> 09:14.136
In fact, I have bad thoughts.

09:15.346 --> 09:16.681
When I moved away from home,

09:17.348 --> 09:19.058
I left behind a kid sister.

09:19.559 --> 09:22.019
She's sick,
and our mother takes care of her alone.

09:22.520 --> 09:24.605
But for some reason,
I don't have a heavy heart.

09:26.440 --> 09:27.942
In fact, I'm a little happier.

09:28.734 --> 09:32.196
Although, I felt a little guilty…
for a while.

09:33.823 --> 09:35.491
That's not a bad thought, Won-jun?

09:37.618 --> 09:38.661
Yeah, it is.

09:39.662 --> 09:42.415
It's super bad.
I've never told anyone before today.

09:43.833 --> 09:44.834
You're the first.

09:54.719 --> 09:55.553
[chuckles]

09:56.304 --> 09:57.221
[laughs]

09:58.806 --> 10:00.766
Hey, what's so funny?
Why are you laughing?

10:01.392 --> 10:02.935
[laughing]

10:05.855 --> 10:08.274
- Uh, what is it?
- Seriously.

10:08.983 --> 10:10.276
Wait. Why are you laughing?

10:10.359 --> 10:11.777
[laughing]

10:11.861 --> 10:15.072
- Not telling.
- Oh, come on. What is it? Tell me, Doona.

10:15.156 --> 10:17.908
- Oh, you're so adorable.
- What?

10:17.992 --> 10:19.994
[emotional music playing]

11:09.001 --> 11:12.213
TIME TO MOVE ON FROM
YOUR PAST RELATIONSHIP AND START ANEW!

11:12.296 --> 11:14.799
SEIZE EVERY
OPPORTUNITY TO CHANGE YOUR FATE

11:22.056 --> 11:23.766
What? Face an enemy?

11:24.433 --> 11:25.935
You don't have any of those, do you?

11:26.018 --> 11:28.729
Exactly. It's all one big superstition.

11:29.313 --> 11:30.815
Do you still have the fortune?

11:31.399 --> 11:33.609
Give it to me. I'll throw it out for you.

11:35.444 --> 11:36.946
[Won-jun] It should be burned.

11:39.281 --> 11:41.200
So what did Doona say about it all?

11:41.283 --> 11:43.452
- [girl] Who do you think you are?
- Oh, what the…

11:43.536 --> 11:45.371
[girl in Portuguese]
I spent all that damn money

11:45.454 --> 11:46.872
for you to learn Korean,

11:46.956 --> 11:48.165
and you cheat on me?

11:48.749 --> 11:50.584
[boy] Whoa. Whoa. Whoa, hey!

11:50.668 --> 11:52.503
- Whoa, whoa!
- [in English] That's fucking mine!

11:52.586 --> 11:55.214
[in Portuguese]
I told you to learn how to communicate,

11:55.297 --> 11:57.466
not to communicate with some bitch.

11:57.550 --> 11:58.467
[boy] Some bitch?

11:59.218 --> 12:02.430
Why are you angry?
I told you she's just a friend!

12:02.513 --> 12:04.265
[in English] Just a friend?
I call bullshit!

12:04.348 --> 12:06.892
You don't hang out with friends
wearing only boxers and socks.

12:07.893 --> 12:08.894
[boy scoffs]

12:10.104 --> 12:11.814
Hey, Dos Santos! You're an ass!

12:12.523 --> 12:13.399
[grunts]

12:13.899 --> 12:15.735
Fuck you, you son of a bitch!
You hear that?

12:15.818 --> 12:18.612
You motherfucker! Get out of here!
You got it?

12:19.989 --> 12:21.907
- [girls scoffs]
- [girl] Whoo!

12:21.991 --> 12:23.159
Thank you.

12:27.455 --> 12:29.206
Hey, what is it? Do you know her?

12:29.290 --> 12:30.666
Uh, no, I don't think so.

12:31.333 --> 12:33.127
I think I mistook her for someone else.

12:36.255 --> 12:37.548
- The fortune.
- Ah.

12:41.427 --> 12:42.970
- Let's go.
- Mm-hmm.

12:50.728 --> 12:51.854
[Won-jun] Jin-ju.

12:53.105 --> 12:53.939
Uh-huh.

13:02.490 --> 13:03.699
[phone ringing]

13:06.452 --> 13:07.536
[girl] What is it?

13:08.496 --> 13:10.456
Ah, shit, that bitch RA!

13:14.627 --> 13:15.795
[yells]

13:16.462 --> 13:17.505
[grunts]

13:19.757 --> 13:21.884
DO NOT BLOCK
FAILURE TO COMPLY WILL RESULT IN EVICTION

13:21.967 --> 13:23.135
Hey! Hey!

13:23.219 --> 13:25.012
Open the door!

13:25.971 --> 13:27.014
[groans]

13:27.097 --> 13:31.727
Our revered comrade Choi I-ra has lead
in penalty points for 13 months now!

13:31.811 --> 13:33.145
You have my respect!

13:33.229 --> 13:35.147
[girls] A round of applause.

13:35.231 --> 13:36.816
- Whoo!
- Yes. Yes.

13:38.567 --> 13:39.652
[chuckles]

13:40.611 --> 13:42.154
PENALTY POINTS FOR MAY
WINNER: CHOI I-RA

13:42.238 --> 13:43.697
WARNING! EVICTION UPON 20 POINTS

13:45.366 --> 13:46.200
[sighs]

13:48.536 --> 13:50.621
I'm being discriminated
because I didn't grow up here,

13:50.704 --> 13:51.872
pure and simple.

13:52.373 --> 13:54.250
I-ra, don't you have any remorse at all?

13:54.333 --> 13:55.167
Ah!

13:55.668 --> 13:57.795
Well, that's what happens
when you spend every night out

13:57.878 --> 13:59.129
getting so drunk.

13:59.255 --> 14:01.841
Or when you decided to smash up
all of those windows in the hallway.

14:01.924 --> 14:02.758
Remember?

14:02.842 --> 14:06.679
Hey, do you remember that time
she hosted the Pig Samba Festival?

14:06.762 --> 14:09.098
[girl laughs]
That was so freaking hilarious.

14:09.181 --> 14:11.392
The fact
that you haven't been kicked out yet

14:11.475 --> 14:13.143
feels like discrimination against us.

14:13.227 --> 14:14.311
[laughing]

14:14.395 --> 14:17.815
I'll have you know I'm single now.
I won't be staying out, getting drunk.

14:17.898 --> 14:19.608
No sleeping at his place anymore.

14:20.317 --> 14:22.611
And there won't be
a Pig Samba Festival this year.

14:22.695 --> 14:23.571
Whoa.

14:24.655 --> 14:26.782
So, um, Buenos Aires and you
finally broke up?

14:26.866 --> 14:27.783
That's right.

14:27.867 --> 14:30.995
Hey, I'll have you know
that's the capital of Argentina.

14:31.078 --> 14:32.371
His name is Dos Santos.

14:32.454 --> 14:34.123
How did you get accepted here?

14:34.206 --> 14:36.750
Ugh, you're seriously so ignorant.
It's unbelievable.

14:36.834 --> 14:38.794
- What a fucking bastard.
- [girl 2] Jeez!

14:39.712 --> 14:41.213
[I-ra] Stay out of my life.

14:43.382 --> 14:45.009
Go die somewhere, you dick!

14:45.092 --> 14:46.719
[crying]

14:49.680 --> 14:51.181
Is she serious right now?

14:55.519 --> 14:56.687
Well, you know,

14:56.770 --> 15:00.399
we should probably take her
on our… well, our group blind date.

15:00.482 --> 15:01.734
That's an odd number.

15:01.817 --> 15:04.320
I can't take… this.

15:05.738 --> 15:09.366
- Haven't they got a friend they can add?
- [crying]

15:17.207 --> 15:18.626
[phone vibrates]

15:21.378 --> 15:22.212
SO-MIN

15:22.296 --> 15:25.925
[So-min] Won-jun, was the goddess
in the lecture hall the real Doona

15:26.008 --> 15:27.217
from Dream Sweet?

15:27.301 --> 15:30.512
[boy] Check out the link Seong-guk posted
in the department group chat.

15:32.056 --> 15:34.058
[mysterious music playing]

15:34.141 --> 15:35.684
DREAM SWEET'S EX-LEAD-SINGER DOONA

15:38.354 --> 15:39.939
[boy 2] Unbelievable that a female idol

15:40.022 --> 15:41.607
is eating in the middle of the night.

15:41.690 --> 15:43.150
What a freaking cushy life she has.

15:43.233 --> 15:45.277
[boy 3] Dream Sweet is falling apart
since Doona left.

15:45.361 --> 15:47.821
[boy 4] Is he a non-celebrity?
That bastard should pay more tax.

15:47.905 --> 15:49.406
[boy 5] I hope this is an edited image.

15:49.490 --> 15:52.368
- [girl] I guess Lee Doona still has fans.
- [girl 2] She's notoriously rude.

15:52.451 --> 15:54.536
There's only a handful of them left.
The loud minority.

15:54.620 --> 15:57.831
[boy 6] If she wants to live like a normal
person, her bank account should match.

15:57.915 --> 16:01.460
[girl 3] She makes all the money she can,
then bails when she feels like it. LOL.

16:01.543 --> 16:04.088
[girl 4] Dream Sweet hasn't been able
to release a studio album

16:04.171 --> 16:06.215
since she deserted them.
Who does she think she is?

16:06.298 --> 16:07.424
[girl 5] Totally a dick move.

16:07.508 --> 16:09.802
- [boy 7] Has she completely retired?
- [boy 8] Fucking bitch.

16:09.885 --> 16:13.722
[boy 9] Nope, she'll be back
once the money runs out. 100%.

16:13.806 --> 16:14.807
[laughs]

16:14.890 --> 16:16.976
LOOK AT HER LIVING A NORMAL LIFE
UNBELIEVABLE

16:18.811 --> 16:19.770
[sighs]

16:20.270 --> 16:21.105
[timer beeps]

16:26.527 --> 16:27.653
[Doona chuckles]

16:31.865 --> 16:32.825
It's super hot.

16:39.915 --> 16:41.875
That picture of us
looked pretty good, hmm?

16:41.959 --> 16:44.378
It looked like an old Hong Kong flick.

16:45.129 --> 16:46.422
Doona, are you doing okay?

16:47.172 --> 16:48.507
Fascinating, isn't it?

16:49.008 --> 16:50.884
We were the only ones in there.

16:52.302 --> 16:54.430
Did our waiter take it then? [sniffs]

16:54.513 --> 16:55.347
Hmm.

16:58.267 --> 16:59.309
Why the long face?

17:02.312 --> 17:04.231
Do you feel your privacy was violated?

17:05.274 --> 17:07.234
No, I just feel bad for you that, uh,

17:08.527 --> 17:10.487
people are talking about you online.

17:12.948 --> 17:13.866
[Doona] Like what?

17:15.034 --> 17:16.243
Are they trash-talking?

17:18.078 --> 17:19.705
They're so mean about it.

17:22.958 --> 17:25.294
You've never looked me up online
until now? [chuckles]

17:26.712 --> 17:28.589
I'm like a dumpster for public trash.

17:30.924 --> 17:32.301
I'm the girl

17:33.802 --> 17:35.471
everyone trash-talks.

17:36.805 --> 17:38.307
They say whatever they think about me.

17:42.394 --> 17:45.314
I've also been told my earnings
have to come from my looks

17:45.397 --> 17:47.191
'cause I have no talent. [sighs]

17:47.775 --> 17:49.276
Luckily, I'm worth a lot.

17:50.778 --> 17:52.488
That makes this worthwhile.

17:54.031 --> 17:55.699
[Won-jun] What? Really? They say all that?

17:56.283 --> 17:58.827
[sighs] Wow, there are
some really annoying fuckers out there.

18:01.622 --> 18:02.790
Mmm, yup.

18:03.332 --> 18:04.541
Don't quit swearing. It's hot.

18:05.125 --> 18:05.959
What?

18:06.043 --> 18:06.919
Swear some more.

18:07.419 --> 18:09.213
- Please do it again.
- What? No.

18:09.922 --> 18:12.883
Hey, how come you never take things
seriously? Stop playing with me.

18:13.425 --> 18:16.386
Anyway, I'm glad to know
you're doing all right.

18:16.470 --> 18:17.596
I'll see you later, then.

18:27.439 --> 18:28.482
[sighs]

18:30.067 --> 18:31.985
[footsteps approaching]

18:32.069 --> 18:33.070
Hey, Doona.

18:34.196 --> 18:36.865
If you ever have to address the public,

18:36.949 --> 18:39.535
or do a press conference
or something in the future,

18:40.911 --> 18:41.954
You'll come with me?

18:43.288 --> 18:45.040
Well, if that's okay.

18:46.875 --> 18:48.627
And what would you say, Won-jun?

18:49.294 --> 18:50.462
That we're just good friends.

18:59.263 --> 19:02.099
Why don't you tell them
that we're more than just friends?

19:07.271 --> 19:09.106
Do you think you could handle it?

19:09.815 --> 19:12.317
- [laughs]
- [sighs] Seriously?

19:13.819 --> 19:14.653
Ah.

19:14.736 --> 19:16.530
[laughing]

19:16.613 --> 19:17.739
Hey, hold on!

19:19.199 --> 19:21.827
I'll come up with you. Hey, hey, wait.

19:23.662 --> 19:25.747
- Be honest, your heart was pounding.
- No, it wasn't.

19:25.831 --> 19:28.000
- That's not what your pupils said.
- Then, they lied.

19:28.083 --> 19:29.459
[Doona laughs]

19:29.543 --> 19:31.378
What would you wear
to the press conference?

19:31.461 --> 19:33.172
[Won-jun] Um… a traditional hanbok.

19:33.255 --> 19:35.257
[Doona laughs]

19:35.340 --> 19:36.675
To a press conference?!

19:36.758 --> 19:38.927
Who wears hanbok to a press conference?

19:47.936 --> 19:49.646
TIME TO MOVE ON FROM
YOUR PAST RELATIONSHIP

19:49.730 --> 19:50.981
CHANGE YOUR FATE

19:57.237 --> 19:58.322
[knock on door]

20:03.035 --> 20:04.077
Dinner.

20:04.161 --> 20:05.704
Okay, thanks. Hmm.

20:11.710 --> 20:13.921
Do you girls use social media at all?

20:14.004 --> 20:16.924
I do have an account.
I don't use it though.

20:17.007 --> 20:19.301
Delete your accounts. No social media.

20:21.220 --> 20:22.137
Yes, sir.

20:24.014 --> 20:24.848
[phone chimes]

20:24.932 --> 20:25.849
[sighs]

20:27.601 --> 20:29.728
WOULD YOU LIKE TO DEACTIVATE
RATHER THAN DELETE?

20:30.562 --> 20:34.191
RECENT SIGHTING OF LEE DOONA EATING
WITH A MAN IN THE MIDDLE OF THE NIGHT

20:34.274 --> 20:35.817
IS SHE CRAZY?

20:39.029 --> 20:41.031
[gentle music playing]

20:53.877 --> 20:54.711
[sighs]

21:03.178 --> 21:05.180
[Doona groans]

21:15.941 --> 21:17.943
[birds chirping]

21:20.112 --> 21:21.655
Wow, the weather is,

21:22.948 --> 21:24.366
in fact, amazing.

21:26.493 --> 21:27.452
[chuckles softly]

21:36.086 --> 21:36.920
Huh?

21:41.008 --> 21:43.051
YOU WILL FACE YOUR ENEMY
AT THE WORST MOMENT

21:43.135 --> 21:44.845
YOU'LL BE AS HELPLESS
AS A MOUSE IS TO A CAT

21:44.928 --> 21:46.138
What? What is this?

21:46.930 --> 21:48.765
I'm positive I gave this to Jin-ju.

21:49.891 --> 21:51.852
Oh, man, this is creepy as heck.

21:59.109 --> 22:00.777
Not today! Knock on wood!

22:03.989 --> 22:04.823
I'll knock twice!

22:04.906 --> 22:06.908
[upbeat music playing]

22:24.384 --> 22:25.594
[Doona] What are you up to?

22:26.803 --> 22:28.805
- Hmm?
- Are you going out?

22:29.681 --> 22:30.515
[Doona] Me?

22:31.933 --> 22:33.101
I got a date.

22:35.437 --> 22:36.646
Who with?

22:37.939 --> 22:39.024
With you.

22:40.567 --> 22:41.401
[Won-jun] What?

22:42.069 --> 22:44.571
We said if the weather was nice,
we'd go on a date?

22:45.280 --> 22:46.156
Oh.

22:47.324 --> 22:48.867
Well, I've got finals coming up.

22:50.744 --> 22:51.787
Hey, listen.

22:51.870 --> 22:53.789
Stop being boring and look at these eyes?

22:53.872 --> 22:56.458
See this eyeliner? I did it perfectly.

22:56.541 --> 22:58.168
Do you think this is easy?

22:58.794 --> 23:00.629
Compared to this, mine is harder.

23:02.672 --> 23:03.548
What will you wear?

23:10.806 --> 23:11.848
How's this, huh?

23:12.349 --> 23:14.518
Oh, I meant to tell you.
You should take some clothes.

23:14.601 --> 23:16.061
Given what happened recently,

23:16.144 --> 23:18.146
you should leave
some men's clothing at your place.

23:18.230 --> 23:20.857
It may deter future stalkers,
so take this.

23:20.941 --> 23:23.235
And… you should take this too.

23:23.318 --> 23:25.195
[phone ringing]

23:25.904 --> 23:26.863
Wait just a minute.

23:28.156 --> 23:29.074
Hey, Yun-taek.

23:29.157 --> 23:31.493
[Yun-taek] Hey, hey, hey, Won-jun,
you've got to help me out.

23:31.993 --> 23:32.911
Why? What happened?

23:32.994 --> 23:35.372
[Yun-taek] I'll tell you
when you get here. Can you come now?

23:35.455 --> 23:36.581
Please come now, okay?

23:37.290 --> 23:38.291
Won-jun, listen to me.

23:38.375 --> 23:40.710
I won't live unless you come.

23:41.545 --> 23:42.838
I'll text you the address.

23:42.921 --> 23:43.922
[line beeps]

23:44.005 --> 23:45.173
Uh, uh…

23:45.257 --> 23:47.592
What? Um, hello?
Yun-taek, answer me. You there?

23:47.676 --> 23:48.510
Hello?

23:49.261 --> 23:50.470
What's going on?

23:50.554 --> 23:51.972
Sorry. I've got to get out of here.

23:52.055 --> 23:54.307
Yun-taek really needs me.
He said it was urgent.

23:54.391 --> 23:55.976
Why can't you just let him die instead?

23:56.059 --> 23:58.645
Um, would you just remember
to lock the door?

23:59.771 --> 24:00.981
I'll be back afterwards.

24:13.118 --> 24:15.162
- [Yun-taek] Anything yet?
- [Jeong-jin] Not yet.

24:18.165 --> 24:19.291
Won-jun, hey!

24:20.542 --> 24:21.376
Yun-taek.

24:23.795 --> 24:26.173
- Was he cute?
- I definitely think I saw some potential.

24:26.256 --> 24:28.091
- He looks really good from behind.
- Let's go.

24:28.175 --> 24:30.427
- [panting]
- Hey, are you all right? I was so worried.

24:30.510 --> 24:32.095
- What's wrong, Yun-taek?
- [Yun-taek] Yeah.

24:32.179 --> 24:34.264
Everything's fine. All good now, buddy!

24:34.347 --> 24:35.557
Oh. Look.

24:40.896 --> 24:41.813
[Yun-taek chuckles]

24:42.647 --> 24:44.065
He's cute as fuck.

24:44.149 --> 24:46.193
- Cute. [coughs]
- He's way cute.

24:46.276 --> 24:47.736
[curious music playing]

25:03.043 --> 25:04.419
[Yun-taek] Sorry about the holdup.

25:04.503 --> 25:06.171
[girl chuckles] Oh, no worries!

25:06.671 --> 25:07.964
[Yun-taek] So, how are you doing?

25:13.094 --> 25:17.641
[Won-jun] I'd forgotten for way too long
that I did, in fact, have an enemy.

25:17.724 --> 25:19.142
[woman yelling]

25:25.732 --> 25:27.400
[yelling]

25:28.860 --> 25:33.323
[woman] Ah, it hurts!
Uh, my belly! I'm dying! I'm dying!

25:33.406 --> 25:34.449
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

25:34.533 --> 25:36.535
- [orchestral music playing]
- [baby crying]

25:36.993 --> 25:38.828
I-RA, 12/31, 11:59 P.M.
WON-JUN, 1/1, 12:00 A.M.

25:38.912 --> 25:41.915
[Won-jun] That was
the beginning of the tragedy.

25:42.916 --> 25:44.417
- [woman] Oh, I've got it.
- [woman 2] Aw.

25:44.501 --> 25:47.546
[woman] Let's have them
marry each other so we can be in-laws.

25:47.629 --> 25:50.215
[woman 2 gasps]
That would be so wonderful.

25:50.298 --> 25:51.716
[woman laughs] Right?

25:56.638 --> 25:58.098
[Won-jun crying]

25:58.723 --> 26:00.433
No. [cries]

26:01.768 --> 26:03.937
[crying]

26:04.020 --> 26:05.689
Stop it.

26:05.772 --> 26:07.691
Stop it. I don't wanna spin anymore.

26:07.774 --> 26:09.317
Start calling me Noona, then!

26:09.401 --> 26:11.987
- [Won-jun cries]
- You better say it or else I'll…

26:14.197 --> 26:15.490
No. No.

26:16.908 --> 26:19.202
[I-ra] Hey, have a bite of this.

26:19.995 --> 26:22.998
I don't want to. Stop!
I don't want any of it! Stop it!

26:23.081 --> 26:25.750
[groans] I told you to stop it.
I don't want any, huh?

26:25.834 --> 26:28.628
How dare you talk to me like that?
I'm your elder. Got it?

26:29.337 --> 26:30.463
Whatever.

26:30.547 --> 26:31.840
Here. Eat some more.

26:44.603 --> 26:46.771
[I-ra] Won-jun, my future husband,

26:46.855 --> 26:48.898
save yourself for me until we meet again.

26:48.982 --> 26:52.068
If you cheat on me, I'll curse you and
your descendants for three generations.

26:52.152 --> 26:53.069
Got it?

26:53.153 --> 26:54.362
I will return.

26:54.446 --> 26:55.697
I will be back.

27:03.330 --> 27:04.706
[I-ra] Lee Won-jun!

27:05.832 --> 27:08.043
[sad trumpet music playing]

27:17.218 --> 27:20.722
[Won-jun] At the age of 12,
Choi I-ra immigrated to Brazil,

27:20.805 --> 27:22.682
leaving me with 1,000 paper cranes,

27:22.766 --> 27:25.518
a curse,
and the impending doom of her return.

27:25.602 --> 27:29.147
Strangely, after her departure,
I finally started to grow taller.

27:29.230 --> 27:30.607
[Yun-taek] Here, have a beer.

27:30.690 --> 27:33.068
You seriously don't recognize me
from anywhere?

27:33.652 --> 27:34.694
No, we never met.

27:34.778 --> 27:37.989
[chuckles] Yangjin Healthcare Center
doesn't ring a bell either?

27:38.073 --> 27:38.990
I've never heard of it.

27:39.074 --> 27:41.534
[gasps] So you've never been
to The Piano Academy either?

27:41.618 --> 27:42.452
Right.

27:43.078 --> 27:45.497
[laughs] Sure, okay! Ah.

27:46.289 --> 27:47.332
I wonder why?

28:19.406 --> 28:20.323
[sighs]

28:36.089 --> 28:37.632
[mysterious music playing]

28:37.716 --> 28:39.718
[light switch clicking]

28:42.762 --> 28:44.764
[breathing shakily]

28:49.060 --> 28:49.894
[I-ra] Love shot!

28:49.978 --> 28:53.606
Hey, Mr. First-Time-That-We've-Met,
you're being very quiet, hmm?

28:53.690 --> 28:55.191
This'll be our first and last meeting.

28:55.275 --> 28:56.484
- That's what I think.
- Uh-huh!

28:56.568 --> 28:57.944
- Mm-hmm!
- [I-ra] Right.

28:58.027 --> 28:59.696
- [chuckles]
- Ha.

28:59.779 --> 29:01.906
- Huh.
- [chuckles]

29:05.952 --> 29:07.203
[girl] Everyone, take one.

29:14.711 --> 29:16.212
- Number one…
- Who's number one?

29:16.296 --> 29:17.505
Yeah, who is it?

29:18.131 --> 29:21.176
- Ha!
- Ooh, it's Choi I-ra.

29:21.259 --> 29:23.636
Okay, number one grab
the face of number four and--

29:23.720 --> 29:25.555
- Who's number four?
- [girl 2] Who is it?

29:25.638 --> 29:27.182
- Ah!
- [laughing]

29:27.265 --> 29:31.436
[Yun-taek] Grabs number four's face
and caresses it while…

29:31.519 --> 29:33.104
[boy] Make it hot.

29:33.188 --> 29:34.189
[girls] Make it hot!

29:34.272 --> 29:35.690
…you kiss him!

29:35.774 --> 29:37.192
Ah!

29:37.275 --> 29:40.653
[all chanting] Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

29:40.737 --> 29:43.239
- [Yun-taek] I love this. This is great.
- [I-ra] All right, then.

29:43.323 --> 29:45.909
Let's see how much longer
you can keep up this act.

29:45.992 --> 29:48.661
- [boy] Kiss!
- [Yun-taek laughs] Kiss!

29:48.745 --> 29:50.121
- [boy] Kiss!
- [girl squeals]

29:50.205 --> 29:51.206
[Yun-taek] Go on.

29:51.289 --> 29:52.499
[girl squeals]

29:52.582 --> 29:54.626
[boy] Whoa!

29:57.962 --> 29:59.964
There they go. They're gonna do it!

30:00.048 --> 30:02.467
Kiss! Kiss! Yeah!

30:02.550 --> 30:03.885
[all] Kiss!

30:03.968 --> 30:05.970
[laughing]

30:08.765 --> 30:09.974
[squeals]

30:10.058 --> 30:11.476
Oh, oh, oh!

30:13.228 --> 30:15.355
Give it a rest, won't you, Choi I-ra?

30:15.438 --> 30:16.731
[Yun-taek] What's happening?

30:16.815 --> 30:19.150
- Punishment means I drink?
- Hey, wait. No. No!

30:19.234 --> 30:20.735
[boy] Won-jun, what are you guys doing?

30:20.819 --> 30:24.531
- [overlapping chatter]
- No, you have to. Stop! You're all mine!

30:24.614 --> 30:27.158
[overlapping chatter]

30:37.126 --> 30:38.294
[sighs]

30:39.379 --> 30:40.713
- [Yun-taek humming]
- [gasps]

30:45.009 --> 30:46.761
[mumbling]

30:46.845 --> 30:47.971
♪ Honey, bunny… ♪

30:48.054 --> 30:50.056
[Doona] So you weren't kidnapped, then?

30:50.139 --> 30:50.974
Oh.

30:53.768 --> 30:55.520
Oh. Kidnapped?

30:55.603 --> 30:56.479
No, actually,

30:57.105 --> 30:58.982
it was a group blind date. [chuckles]

30:59.065 --> 31:00.066
Group date?

31:00.733 --> 31:01.568
Uh-huh.

31:04.445 --> 31:05.738
We met these girls, uh,

31:06.698 --> 31:09.367
and Won-jun was so sensational tonight.

31:09.450 --> 31:10.702
Uh-huh.

31:10.785 --> 31:14.038
The guy was, like, in rare form tonight

31:14.122 --> 31:15.415
and all spruced up.

31:15.498 --> 31:18.960
And the girls' eyes were all
twinkle, twinkle, baby, baby stars--

31:19.043 --> 31:20.128
[chokes]

31:20.211 --> 31:21.546
Ow. Ah.

31:22.130 --> 31:24.215
So why hasn't he
come back from the date yet?

31:24.299 --> 31:25.925
Won-jun? [chuckles]

31:26.843 --> 31:28.344
Won-jun left with this

31:29.220 --> 31:31.055
little sexpot that he met there.

31:31.556 --> 31:32.891
[laughs]

31:32.974 --> 31:36.352
The looks they were giving…
[growls] …were so hot.

31:37.061 --> 31:38.688
Like an explosion, mmm!

31:38.771 --> 31:40.481
So much chemistry.

31:41.190 --> 31:42.150
[sighs]

31:42.233 --> 31:45.278
If I had to bet,
he's not coming home tonight.

31:45.361 --> 31:46.696
You know why?

31:46.779 --> 31:50.366
Because tonight,
that girl is going to just… [snarls]

31:51.075 --> 31:53.536
Uh, you get me. [chuckles]

31:53.620 --> 31:56.289
No way he's coming home. Mm-mm. No way.

31:56.372 --> 31:57.415
You know what though?

31:57.999 --> 31:59.542
I honestly thought

31:59.626 --> 32:02.545
Won-jun was hopeless with girls
until today.

32:03.880 --> 32:06.633
He touched her face like this.
He was smooth.

32:08.134 --> 32:11.804
The way he alternated
between anger and then passion.

32:11.888 --> 32:13.222
And then anger some more.

32:13.932 --> 32:14.849
He's got the idea.

32:14.933 --> 32:17.101
It was impressive to see. Mm-hmm.

32:19.812 --> 32:22.398
So why are you waiting here?
Let's go inside.

32:22.899 --> 32:24.067
That's what I'm doing.

32:24.734 --> 32:25.568
Good night.

32:36.204 --> 32:37.497
[bell jingles]

32:41.626 --> 32:42.460
I'm very sorry.

32:43.795 --> 32:45.088
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

32:45.588 --> 32:47.006
Sorry for the inconvenience.

32:50.593 --> 32:51.678
- Hey!
- [I-ra] What?

32:52.762 --> 32:53.680
[Won-jun grunts softly]

32:54.514 --> 32:56.099
- Hey, Choi I-ra!
- [Ira groans]

32:56.849 --> 32:59.143
- What?
- [Won-jun] Come on. Wake up! Hey!

33:01.062 --> 33:03.022
Here, drink this. [sighs]

33:04.273 --> 33:05.358
[coughs]

33:07.902 --> 33:09.320
[won-jun] And have a bite of this.

33:13.866 --> 33:14.742
[sighs]

33:20.581 --> 33:24.002
Hey, what the hell were you thinking,
trying to kiss me earlier?

33:24.877 --> 33:26.587
A kiss isn't that important.

33:26.671 --> 33:28.756
In Brazil, it's just how you say hi, okay?

33:28.840 --> 33:30.675
Well, we're not in Brazil, okay?

33:30.758 --> 33:32.885
In this country,
the customs are more strict.

33:33.428 --> 33:34.262
[sighs]

33:34.345 --> 33:35.179
- Mmm.
- Ah.

33:35.263 --> 33:36.222
That's a crock of shit!

33:36.305 --> 33:39.058
Otherwise, your friends
wouldn't have acted like we were in Ibiza!

33:39.642 --> 33:41.728
- Sh.
- Just say it.

33:42.353 --> 33:45.481
You recognized me from the beginning,
so why did you act like that?

33:45.565 --> 33:48.067
Let's just say
I'm completely uninterested.

33:49.819 --> 33:50.653
[sighs]

33:51.529 --> 33:53.322
- Hey!
- What?

33:57.452 --> 33:59.537
Tell me that you missed me, Won-jun.

33:59.620 --> 34:02.290
See what I mean?
This is why I didn't wanna say I knew you.

34:02.373 --> 34:05.209
If you sobered up, you should head home.
Where do you live? Is it close?

34:06.044 --> 34:07.545
Sorry to disappoint again.

34:09.380 --> 34:11.632
- I still live in the dorms, huh?
- [Won-jun] Ugh!

34:11.716 --> 34:12.800
- [laughs]
- [Won-jun] Hey.

34:13.676 --> 34:15.636
Cut it out. I need to go now, so let's go.

34:15.720 --> 34:18.431
Didn't you say we can walk together?
[laughs]

34:19.515 --> 34:22.852
You mean to say I have the privilege
of my ex-fiancé taking me home?

34:22.935 --> 34:25.688
Ah! Hey, get off me! Ugh!

34:25.772 --> 34:27.732
- You know you like it!
- No, I don't! Ugh, please!

34:27.815 --> 34:29.484
Hey, stop it!

34:29.567 --> 34:31.986
Ugh, would you quit it?
Give it a rest, huh?

34:32.070 --> 34:34.697
[laughing]

34:36.824 --> 34:38.576
[crying]

34:41.037 --> 34:42.288
Hey, why are you crying?

34:43.664 --> 34:45.374
What's wrong? People are watching?

34:47.960 --> 34:50.713
Just so you know, I got dumped.

34:50.797 --> 34:52.298
[crying]

34:52.381 --> 34:55.009
Dos Santos, that son of a… of a bitch.

34:55.093 --> 34:58.888
All I needed was a new guy to date.

34:58.971 --> 35:02.058
I wanted Dos Santos to feel jealous,
but then you showed up.

35:02.141 --> 35:04.894
Why did it have to be you?

35:04.977 --> 35:06.979
[sobbing]

35:13.486 --> 35:15.404
Why you?

35:15.488 --> 35:16.405
[sighs]

35:19.033 --> 35:19.867
[sighs]

35:31.754 --> 35:33.756
[emotional music playing]

35:54.110 --> 35:55.194
[sighs]

36:39.238 --> 36:40.239
[sighs]

36:44.827 --> 36:45.786
Hmm?

36:51.209 --> 36:52.501
He returns.

36:52.585 --> 36:53.419
[Won-jun] Yeah.

36:57.590 --> 36:58.633
[sighs]

37:02.511 --> 37:03.763
You're still awake, huh?

37:04.639 --> 37:05.473
Mmm.

37:07.808 --> 37:09.435
What are you doing alone out here?

37:10.561 --> 37:11.979
My lights are not working.

37:13.147 --> 37:14.315
It's really dark inside.

37:15.483 --> 37:16.943
There must be a power outage.

37:17.652 --> 37:18.527
Oh, really?

37:21.489 --> 37:22.323
Huh.

37:22.907 --> 37:24.909
The second-floor lights are still working.

37:29.038 --> 37:31.165
Oh, uh, did you hurt your hand?

37:33.292 --> 37:34.126
Oh yeah.

37:35.294 --> 37:38.172
- I must've burned it smoking.
- Let me see.

37:41.884 --> 37:44.345
Ouch. Well, it must have just happened.

37:44.929 --> 37:45.888
Do you have any ice?

37:49.183 --> 37:50.017
In my kitchen.

37:55.606 --> 37:58.734
The refrigerator is still working,
so it's not a full power outage.

37:58.818 --> 38:00.903
Uh, I'll check the breaker panel for you.

38:05.825 --> 38:07.285
So I heard you went on a blind date?

38:08.536 --> 38:09.370
Yeah.

38:12.832 --> 38:14.125
So what do you do on one?

38:15.209 --> 38:17.461
Hmm, nothing unusual.

38:18.045 --> 38:20.172
Drink some beers, couple up,

38:20.756 --> 38:22.049
play childish games.

38:26.429 --> 38:28.055
You really reek of alcohol.

38:29.015 --> 38:29.974
[Won-jun] Yeah.

38:31.017 --> 38:32.226
I had a lot to drink.

38:39.859 --> 38:42.236
You also reek of a women's perfume.
Why is that?

38:43.404 --> 38:45.823
Oh, it's, um, from the girl I was with.

38:49.827 --> 38:51.037
Okay, give me your hand.

39:07.553 --> 39:08.596
That's so weird.

39:09.722 --> 39:11.682
I was perfectly fine earlier tonight.

39:14.935 --> 39:17.980
So why do I suddenly feel pain
just because you've somehow noticed it?

39:19.231 --> 39:20.900
It's just the way it happens.

39:22.318 --> 39:24.445
There are times
you don't even realize you've been hurt.

39:25.404 --> 39:27.573
And as soon as you become aware of it,

39:27.656 --> 39:29.658
you finally notice it and it hurts.

39:29.742 --> 39:30.826
It's strange. I know.

39:35.998 --> 39:37.291
So that's the way it is, then?

39:37.958 --> 39:39.794
Yes, that's the way it is.

39:42.171 --> 39:43.047
[sighs]

39:44.423 --> 39:45.966
Is that the reason I…

39:49.470 --> 39:50.805
I feel this way?

40:36.725 --> 40:38.727
[emotional music playing]

40:49.738 --> 40:51.532
TIME TO MOVE ON FROM
YOUR PAST RELATIONSHIP

40:51.615 --> 40:53.242
SEIZE EVERY OPPORTUNITY
TO CHANGE YOUR FATE

40:53.325 --> 40:56.871
♪ I close my eyes and I see you ♪

41:00.207 --> 41:03.752
♪ I feel my heart beating for you ♪

41:06.797 --> 41:09.842
♪ You take my breath away ♪

41:10.593 --> 41:13.721
♪ Whenever you hold me close ♪

41:13.804 --> 41:15.806
♪ I realized ♪

41:18.142 --> 41:21.395
♪ I can't go back ♪

41:25.024 --> 41:30.070
♪ My everything has started to change ♪

41:32.615 --> 41:37.286
♪ When you appear in my darkness ♪

41:38.913 --> 41:42.708
♪ Looking at the silver light ♪

41:42.791 --> 41:46.504
♪ It was always you and I ♪

41:46.587 --> 41:48.464
♪ Drawn ♪

41:48.547 --> 41:50.341
♪ To you ♪

41:50.424 --> 41:53.427
♪ My moon ♪

41:57.056 --> 42:00.017
♪ I will take time ♪

42:00.100 --> 42:01.769
♪ Or steps ♪

42:01.852 --> 42:05.189
♪ Till we're two and you move back ♪

42:05.272 --> 42:09.068
♪ There's no reason this needs to hide ♪

42:09.151 --> 42:11.946
♪ For me ♪

42:12.655 --> 42:16.700
♪ Even though it's too far ♪

42:16.784 --> 42:19.119
♪ It doesn't matter where you are ♪

42:19.203 --> 42:22.748
♪ My thoughts always go back to you ♪

42:22.831 --> 42:26.252
♪ Because it's you ♪

42:31.674 --> 42:34.218
♪ I hold your hand so tight ♪

42:34.301 --> 42:36.303
♪ I see you ♪

42:39.265 --> 42:43.143
♪ I promise I'll never leave it ♪

42:45.396 --> 42:48.941
♪ You find relief in my answer ♪

42:49.525 --> 42:53.195
♪ I won't ask you to take no more ♪

42:53.279 --> 42:57.032
♪ I'm drawn to you ♪

42:57.116 --> 42:59.994
♪ My moon ♪

43:03.789 --> 43:06.500
♪ I will take time ♪

43:06.584 --> 43:08.460
♪ Or steps ♪

43:08.544 --> 43:12.256
♪ Till we're two and you move back ♪

43:12.339 --> 43:15.634
♪ There's no reason this needs to hide ♪

43:15.718 --> 43:18.637
♪ For me ♪

43:19.346 --> 43:23.309
♪ Even though it's too far ♪

43:23.392 --> 43:25.811
♪ It doesn't matter where you are ♪

43:25.894 --> 43:29.356
♪ My thoughts always go back to you ♪

43:29.440 --> 43:33.360
♪ Because it's you ♪
